Copyright (c) 2026 Michał Weiss and the Roda contributors.

This is DIFFERENT from the licence covering the code in this repository, which
is MIT (see ../LICENSE). The split is deliberate:

  * MIT on the engine, so the scheduler and mode system can be reused freely.
  * CC BY-SA on the courses, so improvements to teaching material come back,
    and so material derived from CC BY-SA sources (Wiktionary/kaikki extracts,
    the UW-Madison "Português para Principiantes" textbook) can be included.

Individual items may carry their own `attribution:` and `license:` fields where
they derive from a third-party source with different terms -- Tatoeba sentences
(CC BY 2.0 FR) and Wikimedia Commons images being the common cases. Those
fields are mandatory for such items and are enforced in CI.

See ../docs/THIRD-PARTY.md for the full list of sources and their terms.
